<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/checklists">Checklists</a> in the menu shows today's checklists where you're working, such as
        <strong>Opening</strong> or <strong>Closing</strong>. That's the location you're clocked in at, or the one you
        signed in to if you aren't clocked in.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Ticking a task">
        <ol>
            <li>Find the checklist. Each one shows when it's <strong>Due</strong>, how many tasks are done, and whether
                it's <strong>Not started</strong>, <strong>In progress</strong>, <strong>Done</strong> or
                <strong>Overdue</strong>.</li>
            <li>Tick the box next to a task once you've done it. Your name and the time appear under it.</li>
            <li>Some tasks ask for more:
                <ul>
                    <li>a <strong>Reading</strong>, such as a fridge temperature. Type the number, then tick the box. If the
                        task has an acceptable range it's shown under the box, and a reading outside it shows a warning
                        before you tick. You can still tick it: <strong>tell a manager straight away</strong>, and use
                        <strong>What did you do? (optional)</strong> to say what you did about it, such as moving the stock
                        to another fridge;</li>
                    <li>a <strong>Note (optional)</strong>. Type it before you tick the box if there's something to say.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Taking a tick back">
        <FluentText>
            Ticked the wrong one? Untick the box. You can take back your own ticks today; a manager can take back anyone's.
            Past days can't be changed. Typed a reading wrong? Untick it and enter it again. Taking back a reading outside the
            range doesn't clear the manager's alert; entering a reading inside the range does.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="On the clock-in terminal">
        <ol>
            <li>Tap <strong>Checklists</strong> at the top of the terminal. It's only there when there's a checklist today.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Who's ticking?</strong>, tap your name and enter your clock-in PIN. This doesn't clock you in or
                out.</li>
            <li>Tick tasks the same way as on your phone. The top of the screen says who you're ticking as, and ticks are
                marked "on the terminal".</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Done</strong> when you've finished, so nobody else ticks in your name.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            If the screen is left alone for two minutes, a <strong>Still there?</strong> message counts down the last 20
            seconds. Press <strong>Keep going</strong> to carry on, or it stops ticking in your name and you'll need your
            PIN again. Wrong PINs count towards the same lockout as clocking in.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Who can tick">
        <ul>
            <li>Anyone on today's rota at the location, and its Managers and Admins.</li>
            <li>Some checklists are just for one position, such as Duty Manager for Closing. If it isn't yours, the boxes are
                greyed out and a message says who can tick it.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
